        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Possible $(a,b,c,d)$: $(2,12,5,30)$, $(4,6,10,15)$, $(6,4,15,10)$ or $(12,2,30,5)$.",
          "worked": "Area ratio, smaller : larger: $24:150=4:25$.\n\nLength ratio: $2:5$.\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}k^2&=\\frac{150}{24}=\\frac{25}{4}\\\\k&=\\frac52=2.5\\\\c&=\\frac52a\\\\d&=\\frac52b\\end{aligned}$$\n\nChoose positive even integers $a,b$ with $ab=24$, so that $c,d$ are integers. The possible tuples are\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}(a,b,c,d)&=(2,12,5,30)\\\\&=(4,6,10,15)\\\\&=(6,4,15,10)\\\\&=(12,2,30,5).\\end{aligned}$$\n\nEach tuple gives $ab=24$, $cd=150$ and $\\frac{c}{a}=\\frac{d}{b}=2.5$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
